Package: libpipnode-core0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libs
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: pipnode flow engine - shared library (headless tier)
 Pipnode is a visual node-based dataflow programming environment.
 .
 This package contains the GTK-free shared library implementing the flow
 engine, message bus, node factory and all node logic. It depends only
 on GLib, JSON-GLib, libsoup and gdk-pixbuf - no graphics toolkit - and
 is what headless installs (pipnode-run) link against.

Package: libpipnode-gui0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libs
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Depends: libpipnode-core0 (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: pipnode flow engine - shared library (GUI tier)
 Pipnode is a visual node-based dataflow programming environment.
 .
 This package contains the GTK-using shared library: the canvas
 renderer, every node's cairo drawing, the settings dialogs, the help
 browser and the panel-layout editor. It links libpipnode-core, GTK 3,
 GtkSourceView, cairo, pango and PLplot.

Package: libpipnode-dev
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libdevel
Depends: libpipnode-core0 (= ${binary:Version}),
         libpipnode-gui0 (= ${binary:Version}),
         libglib2.0-dev,
         libgtk-3-dev,
         libjson-glib-dev,
         libsoup-3.0-dev,
         libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-dev,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: pipnode flow engine - development files
 Headers, pkg-config files and unversioned library symlinks for building
 out-of-tree pipnode plugins or applications that embed the engine.
 .
 Installs pipnode-core.pc (headless tier), pipnode-gui.pc (GUI tier) and
 pipnode.pc (compatibility alias).

Package: pipnode-run
Architecture: any
Section: utils
Depends: libpipnode-core0 (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: pipnode-plugins-starter
Description: pipnode worksheet runner (headless)
 Runs a saved pipnode worksheet without a display: loads the JSON,
 starts the flow, prints debug-node output to stdout and status to
 stderr.
 .
 Designed to live under cron or systemd on a machine with no GTK
 stack installed. Links libpipnode-core only; verify with
 "objdump -p $(command -v pipnode-run) | grep NEEDED".

Package: pipnode-editor
Architecture: any
Section: devel
Depends: libpipnode-core0 (= ${binary:Version}),
         libpipnode-gui0 (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: fonts-font-awesome,
            pipnode-plugins-starter,
            pipnode-plugins-starter-gui
Suggests: xfce4-pipnode-plugin
Description: pipnode visual flow editor
 GTK application: the visual editor where you build, run and inspect
 dataflow worksheets. Also runs as a D-Bus service
 (org.pipas.pipnode.Engine) so panel applets and other clients can drive
 background worksheets.
 .
 Ships the HTML user manual, per-node help pages and the bundled
 example worksheets.

Package: pipnode-plugins-starter
Architecture: any
Section: devel
Depends: libpipnode-core0 (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: pipnode-plugins-starter-gui
Description: pipnode bundled plugins (headless tier)
 The starter set of node plugins shipped with pipnode:
 .
   * network         - HTTP, MQTT, WebSocket, HTTPS tunnel
   * image           - image filters and pixel ops
   * tasmota         - Tasmota power/sensor/switch nodes
   * host-monitoring - CPU, memory, disk, network I/O readouts
   * shell           - shell command runner, tmux monitor
   * sound-effects   - sci-fi clip library player
   * ollama          - local LLM client
 .
 Only the GTK-free logic .so files; pair with pipnode-plugins-starter-gui
 to get the editor-side dialogs for shell, sound-effects and ollama.

Package: pipnode-plugins-starter-gui
Architecture: any
Section: devel
Depends: libpipnode-gui0 (= ${binary:Version}),
         pipnode-plugins-starter (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: pipnode bundled plugins (GUI tier)
 Editor-side companion modules for the two-tier plugins in
 pipnode-plugins-starter: shell, sound-effects and ollama. Each
 companion adds the plugin's custom node-settings dialog to the
 editor; the logic node runs fine without it on headless installs.

Package: xfce4-pipnode-plugin
Architecture: any
Section: xfce
Depends: pipnode-editor (= ${binary:Version}),
         xfce4-panel,
         ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: XFCE panel applet that mirrors a pipnode worksheet
 Adds a pipnode applet to the XFCE panel that renders the panel-band
 widgets (LED displays, lamps, switches) of an associated worksheet
 and forwards clicks back to it.
 .
 Each applet instance owns one worksheet under
 ~/.config/pipnode/panel/. The applet is a thin D-Bus client of the
 pipnode engine (pipnode-editor running in service mode), so a
 worksheet crash cannot take down xfce4-panel.

Package: pipnode
Architecture: all
Section: metapackages
Depends: pipnode-editor,
         pipnode-plugins-starter,
         pipnode-plugins-starter-gui,
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: xfce4-pipnode-plugin
Description: pipnode visual dataflow environment (metapackage)
 Installs the visual editor and the full starter plugin set.
 .
 For a headless install, depend on pipnode-run plus
 pipnode-plugins-starter instead.
